==Old English==

===Etymology===
{{proto|Germanic|sitjan|lang=ang}}, from *{{term||set-}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|sed-|sit|lang=ang}}.  Cognate with Old Frisian [[sitta]], Old High German [[sizzan]] (German [[sitzen]]), Old Saxon [[sittian]] (Dutch [[zitten]]), Old Norse [[sitja]] (Icelandic [[sitja]], Swedish [[sitta]]), Gothic [[𐍃𐌹𐍄𐌰𐌽]].  The PIE root is also the source of Sanskrit {{term|sc=Deva|सीदामि|tr=sīdati|lang=sa}}, Armenian [[nstim]] ‘I sit’, Old Irish [[saidid]] (Irish [[suigh]]), Ancient Greek {{term|ἕζομαι|tr=hezomai|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}, Latin {{term|sedeo|sedeō|lang=la}}, Old Church Slavonic {{term|sc=Cyrs|сѣдѣти|tr=sěděti|lang=cu}} (Russian {{term|сидеть|tr=sidét’|lang=ru|sc=Cyrl}}).

